{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory built a concrete, low-friction pathway, obtained specialty follow-up, and integrated medication, gallbladder, and endoscopy-record gaps. However, the doctor never assessed or safety-netted hematemesis, black or bloody stool, syncope, fever, worsening abdominal pain, confusion, or dehydration; this serious RC1 omission mandates grade 1 despite later handoff success. The doctor also overclaimed that a negative hepatitis C antibody definitively excluded current infection, creating an additional moderate uncertainty-boundary error.",
